// YouVerse data — generated. Events: major documented events per year (World + US).
// Anchors: approximate published figures (UN/World Bank/NASA/NOAA/ITU), interpolated in app.
/* =====================================================================
   YV_EVENTS — HAND-CURATED. READ THIS BEFORE EDITING (annual update).
   The lens: LONG-VIEW MEMORABILITY. Every event is picked and ranked
   by one question — "looking back in 10–20 years, what will this year
   be remembered for?" Cross-category standouts that make someone say
   "oh yeah, THAT happened that year." No category quotas, no filler.
   Order inside each year list IS the rank: the app pins the top 5 and
   date-scatters the rest, so keep the five biggest at the front.
   Density: ~20 events per side (world / us) for a FULL year. The
   in-progress year carries only events that have honestly happened —
   never scheduled milestones or outcomes that haven't landed yet; it
   accrues ~2/month and the app shows a "still being written" line
   while a year is sparse.
   YEAR-END REVAMP (each January): add the closing year's top events
   until both sides are full, re-check its top 5s, then seed the new
   year with whatever has genuinely happened so far.
   ===================================================================== */
